  "term": "substance-induced persisting amnestic disorder",
  "definition": "Substance-induced persisting amnestic disorder is a memory disorder in which a person has trouble forming new memories or recalling past ones because of the lasting effects of substance use. The memory problem continues longer than the usual period of intoxication or withdrawal.",
